From b6d31ddf71ff815f0e47623fb130c84a57f133f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bmatusiak <bmatusiak@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:50:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fido2: a tunnel connect clears the duplicate mark of an
 unfinished request

A request packet that arrives through the WebAuthn tunnel is dropped as a
duplicate when its opt3 is not above the last one taken
(last_request_opt3), and the mark is cleared only when a request's final
packet is handled. A request that never reaches its final packet - the
browser cancelled the next ceremony, the page was closed - leaves the
mark set. A host numbers its packets from 1 again after it connects (a
new page), so its next requests are dropped with an empty success until
its numbers pass the old mark. 3.0.4 kept the mark in
packet_buffer_details[3], which wipetasks() cleared.

A tunnel connect (OKCONNECT) starts a new transit session; it now clears
the mark. A repeated packet inside one request is still dropped.
---
 fido2/ok_extension.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fido2/ok_extension.cpp b/fido2/ok_extension.cpp
index 5e3eac0..cf41b4e 100644
--- a/fido2/ok_extension.cpp
+++ b/fido2/ok_extension.cpp
@@ -201,6 +201,10 @@ int16_t bridge_to_onlykey(uint8_t *_appid, uint8_t *keyh, int handle_len, uint8_
         outputmode = DISCARD; // Discard output
         if (cmd == OKCONNECT && !CRYPTO_AUTH) {
             large_buffer_offset = 0;
+            // Every OKCONNECT makes a new transit key below, so no packet sealed
+            // before it continues a request: the duplicate mark of a request that
+            // never reached its final packet is cleared with it.
+            last_request_opt3 = 0;
             // Set time if not already set
             set_time(client_handle);
             memset(ecc_public_key, 0, sizeof(ecc_public_key));
-- 
